{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-511", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/511", "wordCount": 1553, "segments": [{"start": 6.0, "text": "Hello, I'm Tim Hatcher an"}, {"start": 8.0, "text": "engineer on the WebKit Team."}, {"start": 10.0, "text": "I'm going to talk about"}, {"start": 11.0, "text": "Supporting Dark Mode in Web"}, {"start": 13.0, "text": "Content."}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "When macOS Mojave introduced"}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "Dark Mode, users and developers"}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "naturally began to ask about web"}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "Over the decades web content has"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "traditionally been light in"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "color leading to a very bright"}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "experience when mixed among"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "newly Dark Mode aware apps."}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "The WebKit team has been working"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "to standardize a way for"}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "developers to style web content"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "for Dark Mode, which I'm happy"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "to announce is available in"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "Safari 12.1 on macOS Mojave and"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "with iOS 13's system wide dark"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "appearance, you will see the"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "same Dark Mode styling for web"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "content in Safari for iOS."}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "Throughout this video I'll be"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "using Safari in my examples, but"}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "this support is not just"}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "available in Safari."}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "It is also available in mail and"}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "in your app when showing content"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "in web views."}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "There are three areas I want to"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "cover in this video."}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "One, general styling support for"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "Dark Mode on the web."}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "Two, some specific cases that"}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "apply to email messages."}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "And, three, tools you can use to"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "debug web content in Dark Mode."}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "Let's get started."}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "I've been working on a new blog"}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "to document some recent trips"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "I've taken around California."}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "While designing the site to be"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "responsive for mobile and"}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "desktop visitors, this would be"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "a good time to add support for"}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "Dark Mode."}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "Dark mode can be viewed as a"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "progression of responsive web"}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "design, another way to adapt to"}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "the circumstances of the device."}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "It is important to note that"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "Safari and WebKit will not auto"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "darken your content."}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "As the web developer, you are in"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "control of how your content will"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "appear to users using the dark"}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "system appearance."}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "Let's take a look at how we can"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "transform this light page design"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "into a Dark Mode ready site."}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "The main way to signal that your"}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "content supports Dark Mode is to"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "adopt the new color scheme style"}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "property currently being"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "specified for inclusion in the"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "CSS standard."}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "Specifying the values light and"}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "dark on the root element lets"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "the rendering engine known both"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "modes are supported by the"}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "document."}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "This changes the default text"}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "and background colors of the"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "page to match the current system"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "appearance, standard form"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "controls, scrollbars and other"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "named system colors also change"}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "their look automatically."}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "Let's take a look at how adding"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "that property to my blog"}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "affected things."}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "You can see the background color"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "changed from white to black and"}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "most of my text completely"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "disappeared into the black"}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "background; that was not what I"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "was expecting."}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "Let's take a look at some of the"}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "style rules for this page to see"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "what is happening."}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "Here are the main style rules"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "for the affected areas of the"}, {"start": 196.0, "text": "page."}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "For the text that disappeared"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "the black was being set as the"}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "text color on the body."}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "I also have a dark gray text"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "color for the level 1 headings,"}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "which doesn't have a high enough"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "contrast with the black"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "background."}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "By default, the text color of"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "the body will be black and light"}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "mode."}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "Since that is what I wanted on"}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "this page I can just delete the"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "color property override from my"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "style sheet."}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "Now that I'm using the color"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "scheme property, the default"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "text and background color will"}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "both automatically change to the"}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "Dark Mode values."}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "For the other colors in my style"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "sheet that I want to keep, I can"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "use something called CSS custom"}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "properties otherwise known as"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "CSS variables to centrally"}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "define them for use throughout"}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "my site style sheets."}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "Using CSS variables makes it"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "very easy to later adapt the"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "style sheet for Dark Mode."}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "Let's see how that will work."}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "We simply take the color values"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "and move them to a central place"}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "like the root element rule we"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "added for the color scheme"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "earlier."}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "For these colors we define a"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "variable name signified by a"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "double hyphen prefix."}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "Now we can return to the"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "original style rules where I am"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "still using the static color"}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "values and change them to use"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "the variables we defined"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "referencing them by name using"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "the VAR function which looks"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "like this."}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "This style sheet is now ready to"}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "support a dark color scheme."}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "Like responsive design"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "breakpoints for different device"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "widths, we can use a media query"}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "to conditionalize for Dark Mode."}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "Specifically, if the user"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "currently prefers a dark color"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "scheme."}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "We can override the same CSS"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "variables we defined earlier for"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "light mode with Dark Mode"}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "appropriate color values."}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "Now let's take a look at what"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "the page looks like with these"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "changes applied."}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "We go from this where we only"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "added the color scheme property"}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "to this where the text and"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "header colors properly adapt to"}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "the dark appearance, but what"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "about images?"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "Like the hero picture here of"}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "the Mojave Desert."}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "The Mojave Desert image is"}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "included by an image element"}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "that is sourcing a JPEG on my"}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "server."}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "We can easily adapt this code"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "using another responsive design"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "technique."}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "Specifically, the picture"}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "element, which is a great way to"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "source multiple versions of an"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "image based on various device"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "characteristics using the same"}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "media queries."}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "Here I specify an alternate"}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "image of the Mojave Desert at"}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "night using the same media query"}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "that was used earlier for the"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "Dark Mode colors I can"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "conditionally load a night image"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "for users that prefer a dark"}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "color scheme."}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "So we go from this where I was"}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "using one image for both color"}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "schemes to this where the desert"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "image is adapted to the dark"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "appearance and now the site is"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "ready for both dark and light"}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "appearances."}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "To recap you want to use the new"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "color scheme property to declare"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "support for light and Dark"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "Modes."}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "This informs the rendering"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "engine what color schemes your"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "content was designed for so it"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "can adapt the default colors and"}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "controls to match."}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "When the default colors are not"}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "enough, use the prefers-color-scheme media query"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "for custom values."}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "You can use the same media query"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "along with other responsive"}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "images in the picture element"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "for Dark Mode ready sources and"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "consider using CSS variables"}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "when adopting color schemes."}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "It will be easier to maintain"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "both appearance modes across"}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "your content."}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "That brings us to Dark Mode and"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "email messages."}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "Just like mail in macOS Mohave"}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "simple email messages composed"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "directly in mail on iOS 13 are"}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "ready to go in both light and"}, {"start": 444.0, "text": "dark appearances even if they"}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "include in-line image"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "attachments like you see here."}, {"start": 450.0, "text": "This is the case because of"}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "mail's auto darkening"}, {"start": 453.0, "text": "transformations that get applied"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "to these simple email messages."}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "However, if you are an email"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "template designer creating"}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "designs for a campaign that"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "includes remotely loaded images,"}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "you will need to adopt the same"}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "styling techniques I covered"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "earlier for web content."}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "Without adopting the color"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "scheme property mail will"}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "display your email message in"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "the light appearance and will"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "not employ any auto darkening"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "transformations that simple"}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "email messages receive."}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "Here is the same email message"}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "with Dark Mode styling including"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "the color scheme declaration."}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "It is now perfectly adapted to"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "the dark system appearance."}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "To recap simple email messages"}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "will auto darken even if they"}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "include in-line image"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "attachments and rich email"}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "messages with remote images like"}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "custom email marketing campaigns"}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "will use the light color scheme"}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "by default."}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "You can declare support for the"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "dark color scheme in your"}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "marketing email messages and use"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "the media query for custom color"}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "and image customizations."}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "Now let's talk about tools to"}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "debug Dark Mode content"}, {"start": 526.0, "text": "specifically Web Inspector."}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "In macOS, we added the dark"}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "appearance to Web Inspector when"}, {"start": 533.0, "text": "your system is in Dark Mode."}, {"start": 535.0, "text": "This was a very popular request"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "from web developers, and I'm"}, {"start": 538.0, "text": "very happy we have it now."}, {"start": 541.0, "text": "Not only did we add the dark"}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "appearance there are a couple"}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "tools to help you debug your own"}, {"start": 546.0, "text": "content in Dark Mode."}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "The first is a new color scheme"}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "toggle in the elements tab that"}, {"start": 552.0, "text": "will change the page appearance"}, {"start": 554.0, "text": "without requiring you to toggle"}, {"start": 556.0, "text": "the entire system appearance"}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "every time."}, {"start": 559.0, "text": "So if you like using Dark Mode,"}, {"start": 561.0, "text": "you can quickly test how your"}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "pages will look in the light"}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "appearance with this button."}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "Like before the style sidebar"}, {"start": 571.0, "text": "shows any rules that match for"}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "the selected element including"}, {"start": 575.0, "text": "any media queries."}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "In this case, you can see the"}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "prefers color scheme media query"}, {"start": 581.0, "text": "definitions of color variables"}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "on the WebKit.org site."}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "And that is Dark Mode and Web"}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "Inspector."}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "Check out some of the other"}, {"start": 590.0, "text": "Safari and WebKit sessions for"}, {"start": 592.0, "text": "details about other great new"}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "features in Web Inspector for"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "Safari 13."}, {"start": 598.0, "text": "In summary, remember that web"}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "pages and rich email messages"}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "need to opt into Dark Mode."}, {"start": 603.0, "text": "Safari and WebKit will not auto"}, {"start": 605.0, "text": "darken your content."}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "For simple email messages you"}, {"start": 609.0, "text": "don't have to worry."}, {"start": 610.0, "text": "Mail darkens them to match the"}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "system appearance automatically"}, {"start": 614.0, "text": "and now you can use Web"}, {"start": 616.0, "text": "Inspector to test your content"}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "in light and Dark Modes with the"}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "new color scheme toggle in the"}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "elements tab."}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "I look forward to seeing what"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "you will do with this support"}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "and how your sites and apps will"}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "look in Dark Mode on Mac and"}]}
